A||||12||skitime||Whats up with a SUV Indy pace car?||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||05-29-2001||10:02 AM||||I think the Indy officials are insulting all the former pace cars (including our Fiero) by having  a SUV as a pace car.  Isn't Indy all about racing and sports cars.  I was offended by the whole idea.  What next year a pickup truck? Give me a break!<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever2||05-29-2001||01:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Isn't Indy all about racing and sports cars.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Oh, I don't know.  Isn't racing all about finding new technologies and advancements to use in production passenger cars?  And look at the improvements in SUV's in recent years!  Since the Jeep (which was shortened from Jeepie, which was taken from "G.P.", which I believe meant General Purpose), they've come a long way.  If they could make it faster, I wouldn't mind if they used a Hummer for the pace car.<P>BTW, here's a pic of me with my new friend...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pace_car_&_me.jpg"> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000002||FieroLisa||05-29-2001||01:37 PM||||Chuck, I really do love your photo-editing skills! I do have a pic of me standing next to the Bravada, but I don't have a scanner anywhere near me, so....<P>Actually I'd be scared to pace the race in that car... I was in it at about 80 mph around the track and scared it was gonna roll over!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||05-29-2001||02:25 PM||||I think the 270hp I6 engine in the Bravada would class it in enough power.  Olds probably sup'd it up for being a pace car so it was probably well over 300hp.  Not to sure though, anyone have the specs?<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||05-29-2001||02:53 PM||||Well there are probably some pretty powerful tractor trailer trucks with awesome engines with turbos and cool paint jobs too.  Maybe next year. Lets get some minivans in too. I am sure they can get some hot engines in them too.  My point was that I always felt that the Indy was to showcase cars, not trucks, SUV, motorcycles or tractor trailers.  I was disappointed because a tradition was broken.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||p4n1c||05-29-2001||03:01 PM||||My car and most of the other ones used as indy pace cars were the size of small pickups, SUVs and minivans, so maybe they thought noone would notice.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I think they were doing it to give Oldsmobile it's last time at Indy.  They have been very prominent with pace cars and with the Aurora powered indy car.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000006||kslish||05-29-2001||03:01 PM||||I was sort of confused by the whole thing myself, but I understand it sort of now because of all the sponsership money involved.<P>It's Oldsmobile's last year in the race due to GM phasing out the line (the Olds Aurora Indy V8 engine will probably have a different name next year, my bet is it'll be called a Cadillac Northstar), and they already used the Aurora last year to pace the race.<P>So basically, GM probably waved enough money at the Brickyard officials (remember, the 500 isn't the cash cow it once was with sponsership money due to the IRL/CART split) and they let it be.<P>If Cadillac paces the race next year (I betting on this also if the GM Indy engine is called a Northstar) I just hope Cadillac has enough sense to pace the race with their upcoming Evoq roadster (basically a Northstar powered Vette) and not the Escalade next year.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ken S.<BR>||||reg||1
