Z||000008||rogergarrison||05-29-2001||04:40 PM||||I have a friend that has a 1966 ford Econoline van, Its got a 502 cu chevy and prob would outrun an indy car. LOL<P>(even though its lowered and top chopped a foot, still prob dont corner worth a damn though) Im sure hed like to be a pace car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||sjp777||05-29-2001||09:12 PM||||Could it be that the auto industry is run by a bunch of whores? What better way to promote a vehicle than in front of half a million people? Not to mention the tv audience<P>Everybody and their brother wants a truck, SUV or minivan. The auto industry knows it. Hell, they created the demand by saturating us with ads showing how active and sporty we would all be if only we had an Expedition to take us and our kayaks to the river.<P>It doesn't matter to them if 95% of them never get out of suburbia. These vehicles are spendy and highly profitable. Why make 2 cars when you can realise the same profit margin on 1 SUV.<P>If you need a work truck or a minivan to cart the kids and groceries around, that's fine. But just about 2 out of 3 of these I see on the road only contain the driver, and they are far to clean and scratch free to have ever been off the road.<P>Hopefully, this lame fad too shall pass.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">    <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||13
